A||||6||Phantom Rage||88 upper ball joints?||||5||
Z||000000||Phantom Rage||07-19-2000||08:55 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I was about to put in my new lowering springs/shocks/struts, when I noticed my outer tie rod boot and upper ball joint boot were severely cracked.  They look pretty contaminated.  I called around to get prices. All the major parts stores carried the outer tie rods, but none had the upper ball joints.  <P>Where does one find 88 upper balljoints?  I know The Fiero Store has them but they seem a bit expensive, any alternatives?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">TIA <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||PJ||07-19-2000||09:54 PM||||Curse of the '88's strikes again. I've always got mine from the dealer (hey, I spend so much money there I get 25% off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">). If the originals are still in there you'll have to drill out the rivets that retain them. The GM parts come with nuts and bolts to attach the new pieces.<P>BTW I just tried getting Delco front brake caliper rebuild kits. No longer available. I had to buy the rear kits for more money (same piston diameter). Shipped from MI no less. I guess they won't be around much longer either.<P>Don'tcha just love ownin' an '88? I do. I have two.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||07-19-2000||10:15 PM||||The part number for the 88 upper front ball joints is:  17988889<P>You can get them for $36.49 + s/h @<P> <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/</A> <P>That is where I got my last set.<P><P>------------------<BR>Paul, Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phantom Rage||07-21-2000||07:39 PM||||Thanks guys, been busy for a few days.  Wow, I was calling everyone today trying to find those suckers for a little less.  <P>Yeah your right PJ the 88 does strike again. Sometimes I almost wish I got a pre 88, but I still love my yellow banana <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Pherder that is a great price on the upper ball joints.  Do you know the part number for the outer tie rod ends as well?  <P>I must admit though Pherder, I am a little scared to use their service.  I can't even find their telephone number.  I'll take your word though, since you seem to be happy with them.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000004||fieroparts.com||07-21-2000||08:32 PM||||Sorry to report as of today all 88 upper ball joints are no longer avalable from GM<BR>I placed an order this past monday for 40<BR>and was told by my GM guys I'm only getting<BR>4 total. Good old GM!<P><BR>tim<BR>check out the cool fiero on our web site <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroparts.com</A> ||||reg||9
Z||000005||pherder||07-21-2000||09:49 PM||||Phantom Rage,<P>I do have one problem with them and that is the rain gutter I purchased thru their site.<P>Since it would not fit the box they wanted to use, they bent the @!#$!#@ out of it to make it fit!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>They have responded back to my request to return it BUT it has been sitting at a friend's shop for 3 weeks waiting for UPS to pick it up.  They have suppostly issued a "call tag" for it back on June 27th.  I just sent them another email wanting to know status.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>At this time, I wouldn't recommend them.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Paul, Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT||||reg||8
Z||000006||fiero56||07-21-2000||11:39 PM||||Contact Rodney Dickman about the outer tie-rod ends. I don't remember the price, but he had some at Ed Parks swap meet in April, and I remember the price being very good.||||reg||1
